391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 198 0 R
/T (\(4\) Tomographic Reconstruction Constraints: Current hospital pipelines rely heavily on techniques like Filtered Back Projection \(FBP\) or Algebraic Reconstruction Techniques \(ART\) to build 3D shapes from 2D X-rays. These methods require high doses of radiation to capture enough angles and tend to struggle heavily with signal noise. )
/E (\(4\) Tomographic Reconstruction Constraints: Current hospital pipelines rely heavily on techniques like Filtered Back Projection \(FBP\) or Algebraic Reconstruction Techniques \(ART\) to build 3D shapes from 2D X-rays. These methods require high doses of radiation to capture enough angles and tend to struggle heavily with signal noise. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 198 0 R
/T (The Domain Overlap: PINNs have been massively successful in fully resolved 3D environments. However, trying to apply PINNs directly to 2D projections to figure out both the 3D geometry and the fluid physics at the exact same time is a highly complex inverse problem that hasn't been explored much. )
/E (The Domain Overlap: PINNs have been massively successful in fully resolved 3D environments. However, trying to apply PINNs directly to 2D projections to figure out both the 3D geometry and the fluid physics at the exact same time is a highly complex inverse problem that hasn't been explored much. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
