433 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 201 0 R
/T (The crossover between deep learning, fluid mechanics, and medical imaging is moving incredibly fast. Classical Computational Fluid Dynamics \(CFD\) gives us extremely accurate simulations, but it has a major flaw. It absolutely requires perfect 3D geometries and strict boundary conditions to work. In this chapter, we look back at how physics-driven deep learning has evolved. We also explain exactly why it makes sense to skip traditional tomographic reconstruction when dealing with clinical blood flow. )
/E (The crossover between deep learning, fluid mechanics, and medical imaging is moving incredibly fast. Classical Computational Fluid Dynamics \(CFD\) gives us extremely accurate simulations, but it has a major flaw. It absolutely requires perfect 3D geometries and strict boundary conditions to work. In this chapter, we look back at how physics-driven deep learning has evolved. We also explain exactly why it makes sense to skip traditional tomographic reconstruction when dealing with clinical blood flow. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
434 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 201 0 R
/T (2.2 Physics-Informed Neural Networks \(PINNs\) )
/E (2.2 Physics-Informed Neural Networks \(PINNs\) )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
435 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 201 0 R
/T (When it comes to scientific machine learning, Physics-Informed Neural Networks \(PINNs\) changed everything. Raissi, Perdikaris, and Karniadakis formally introduced them in 2019. Standard neural networks act like data-driven black boxes. They map inputs to outputs without actually understanding the physical world. As a result, if you give them sparse or noisy data, they spit out physically impossible predictions. )
/E (When it comes to scientific machine learning, Physics-Informed Neural Networks \(PINNs\) changed everything. Raissi, Perdikaris, and Karniadakis formally introduced them in 2019. Standard neural networks act like data-driven black boxes. They map inputs to outputs without actually understanding the physical world. As a result, if you give them sparse or noisy data, they spit out physically impossible predictions. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 201 0 R
/T (PINNs fix this. They act as universal function approximators that weave physical laws right into the learning phase. We usually express these laws as partial differential equations \(PDEs\). In fluid mechanics, we use the Navier-Stokes equations to enforce the conservation of mass, momentum, and energy. )
/E (PINNs fix this. They act as universal function approximators that weave physical laws right into the learning phase. We usually express these laws as partial differential equations \(PDEs\). In fluid mechanics, we use the Navier-Stokes equations to enforce the conservation of mass, momentum, and energy. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
