/T (The results failed spectacularly. The Multi-Layer Perceptron did manage to draw smooth color gradients for the hidden pressure, but those gradients had nothing to do with the actual fluid velocity. Because we removed the rules for mass and momentum conservation, the network created completely impossible flow lines. It just drew a lazy, distorted oval, with velocity vectors shooting randomly outside the physical boundaries. This clearly shows that you absolutely need the physics-informed loss function to map real flow dynamics. )
