/P 215 0 R
/T (The network did manage to lower its internal loss numbers, but looking at the actual physical output revealed a major mathematical wall. A single projection angle just ruins too much spatial depth. To keep its data loss low, the AI took a shortcut. It drew a generic, featureless pressure gradient and a very basic spiral in the center. It completely failed to spot the true, uneven 3D vortex of the aneurysm. This proves that trying to map complex 3D fluid dynamics from a single angle is an ill-posed inverse problem, which is exactly why we need to use multi-angle orthogonal projections. )
/E (The network did manage to lower its internal loss numbers, but looking at the actual physical output revealed a major mathematical wall. A single projection angle just ruins too much spatial depth. To keep its data loss low, the AI took a shortcut. It drew a generic, featureless pressure gradient and a very basic spiral in the center. It completely failed to spot the true, uneven 3D vortex of the aneurysm. This proves that trying to map complex 3D fluid dynamics from a single angle is an ill-posed inverse problem, which is exactly why we need to use multi-angle orthogonal projections. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
