628 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (In this chapter, we tested the performance and physical limits of our PINN setup across six specific experiments. Our first few stress tests \(Experiments 1-3\) showed exactly why we needed the 8-layer architecture. They also proved the network could stay physically accurate even when missing massive amounts of data, just by relying on the Navier-Stokes equations. In Experiments 4 and 5, we saw the network act as a smart mathematical denoiser. By bumping up the PDE loss weighting, it easily handled 10% Gaussian noise. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (Finally, we tested if the network could figure out 3D depth directly from 2D shadows. Experiment 6, which used a single-axis projection, exposed a major mathematical flaw. The extreme loss of depth led to a generic, featureless reconstruction. We wrote a multi-angle orthogonal projection framework to beat this issue. We cannot run it right now because standard GPUs do not have enough VRAM, but the code is fully finished. We now have a physics-driven pipeline ready to go as soon as we move to a High-Performance Computing \(HPC\) cluster. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
