647 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 220 0 R
/E (Mixing PINNs with the Forward Radon Transform is a big step for medical computing. Right now, the medical process is broken up: radiologists take 2D pictures, engineers build 3D meshes, and supercomputers run fluid simulations for days. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
648 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 220 0 R
/E (By forcing deep learning models to follow the laws of mass and momentum, we can pull deep 3D physical insights straight from flat 2D images. This project proves that the future of clinical blood flow analysis is not about building heavier, artifact-prone reconstruction algorithms. It is about using highly efficient, physics-aware AI. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
