/Title (The crossover between deep learning, fluid mechanics, and medical imaging is moving incredibly fast. Classical Computational Fluid Dynamics \(CFD\) gives us extremely accurate simulations, but it has a major flaw. It absolutely requires perfect 3D geometries and strict boundary conditions to work. In this chapter, we look back at how physics-driven deep learning has evolved. We also explain exactly why it makes sense to skip traditional tomographic reconstruction when dealing with clinical blood flow.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1884 0 R
>>
endobj
1889 0 obj
<<
/Title (2.2 Physics-Informed Neural Networks \(PINNs\))
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1882 0 R
/Prev 1884 0 R
/First 1894 0 R
/Last 1895 0 R
/Count -2
/Next 1885 0 R
>>
endobj
1890 0 obj
<<
/Title (Applying PINNs to fluid dynamics took a massive step forward with "Hidden Fluid Mechanics" \(HFM\). Raissi et al. published this framework in Science in 2020. Normal CFD needs you to define exact inlet velocities, outlet pressures, and wall boundaries. HFM avoids this completely. It uses deep learning to pull out hidden states just by looking at flow snapshots and applying the Navier-Stokes equations.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1886 0 R
/Next 1896 0 R
>>
endobj
1891 0 obj
<<
/Title (perfect 3D point cloud. In a real-world clinic, you almost never have that kind of perfect 3D data, which creates a major roadblock for deploying this tech.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1886 0 R
/Prev 1897 0 R
>>
endobj
